IP addresses are unique addresses that identify devices connected to the internet or local network. It's sort of a sequence of numbers.
IP addresses; It is divided into two general and hidden. For example, when connecting to the Internet from home, your modem has a public IP that everyone can see, while your computer has a hidden IP that will be transferred to your modem.
The easiest way to find the public IP address of the router is "What's my IP" on Google?
Finding the hidden IP address depends on the platform used:
Type "cmd" command in the search field.
The network is selected and the IP information appears.
Click the "i" in the circle next to the network you are on.
Also, if you want to find someone else's IP address; the easiest among alternative routes; It is the command prompt method on Windows devices.
On the command screen that appears, write the "ping" command and the address of the website you want to watch, and then press the "Enter" key. After all, you can reach the IP address of the site you wrote the address of.
In order to determine the geographical location of the address of an IP address, you can use the "ip query" method. Inquiry result; gives the relevant city, region, zip code, country name, ISP, and time zone.
