When the flywheel of the diesel engine rotates, the speed measuring head installed on the flywheel shell generates a pulsed voltage signal, and the voltage value is sent to the electronic speed control board. If the speed is lower than the preset value of the electronic speed control board, the electronic speed control board outputs.
The coil of the speed measuring head can be tested by using the ohm gear of the multimeter to detect the two terminals of the coil. The resistance value is generally between 100-300 ohms, and the terminals are insulated from the shell of the speed measuring head.
The resistance value is generally between 7-8 ohms. When the power generation needs to run without load, the voltage value that the electronic speed control board outputs to the electronic actuator Generally between 6-8VDC, this voltage value will increase with the increase of load, when fully loaded, generally between 12-13VDC.
