What are differences between gasoline outboard engine and diesel outboard engine? News
Gasoline outboard motor generally injects gasoline into the intake pipe to mix with air to form a combustible mixture and then enter the cylinder. Diesel outboard engine generally injects diesel directly into the engine cylinder through the fuel injection pump and nozzle, and evenly mixes with the compressed air in the cylinder, spontaneously ignites under high temperature and high pressure, and pushes the piston to do work.
The gasoline consumption is high, so the fuel economy is poor (full throttle fuel consumption of Yamaha 60hp two-stroke gasoline outboard is 24L/h). B.
B. Diesel outboard engine has the characteristics of high power, long life and good dynamic performance. It emits 45% lower greenhouse gases than gasoline engines, and also lowers carbon monoxide and hydrocarbon emissions.
D. The torque of the diesel outboard engine is not only larger than that of the gasoline engine of the same displacement, but also the speed range corresponding to the large torque is wider than that of the gasoline engine, that is to say, the low-speed torque of the ship using the diesel outboard engine is larger than that of the gasoline engine of the same displacement. Much easier to start with heavy loads.
Disadvantages of diesel outboards: The speed is lower than the gasoline outboard (the rated speed of the HC60E four-stroke diesel outboard is 4000r/min), the mass is large (the net weight of the HC60E four-stroke diesel outboard is 150kg), and the manufacturing and maintenance costs are high (because the fuel injection pump and fuel injection The machining accuracy of the machine is required to be high). Large emission of harmful particulate matter.
In response to this series of problems, China government has immediately introduced many relevant policies for diesel engine emissions. Among them, high-pressure common rail diesel engines with National III and Euro III emissions in the diesel generator set market are becoming more and more popular in the market.
The advantages of high-pressure common rail diesel engines are low fuel consumption, high reliability, long life, and high torque. Diesel engines with common rail emit much less harmful gases than engines without common rail (especially less CO), so they are environmentally friendly compared to gasoline engines.
The main causes of water leakage are that broken or tilted blades of the fan, during operation, cause the radiator to be injured, or the radiator is not fixed, which cause the diesel engine to crack the joint of the radiator during operation. Or the cooling water contains impurities and excessive salt and the pipe wall is seriously corroded and damaged, etc.
