In the process of using the crusher, if there is a fault, how to deal with it?
Vibration crusher motor is directly connected to the crushing device, which is simple and easy to maintain. However, if the two are not well connected in the assembly process, it will cause the overall vibration of the crusher.
The reason is that the two supporting surfaces of the rotor shaft are not in the same plane. A piece of copper sheet can be mounted on the underside of the bearing pedestal, or an adjustable wedge iron can be added on the underside of the bearing to ensure that the two shaft heads are concentric.
The original balance was upset. After motor repair, dynamic balance test should be done to ensure the overall piece balance.
Too much, too little or too old lubricating oil in the bearing is also the main cause of bearing overheating damage, therefore, according to the requirements of the user's manual to fill the lubricating oil timely and quantitatively, the general lubrication space is 70% to 80% of the bearing space, too much or too little is not conducive to bearing lubrication and heat transfer.
The jam of crusher is one of the common faults in the crusher use, which may be the problems in the mold design, but more due to improper operation. The feeding speed is too fast, the load increases, resulting in blockage.
The discharge pipeline is not unobstructed or blocked, feeding is too fast, the crusher's air outlet will be blocked. Improper matching with the conveying equipment will cause the wind of outlet pipe weakened or no wind after blocking.
While using, many users face the problem of strong vibration, which affects the operation. The following is the reason for the strong vibration and the solution:
When its weight difference is more than 5 grams, the crusher will run strong vibration. The solution is to adjust the position of the hammers to ensure that the weight same or difference between the two corresponding groups of hammers does not exceed 5 grams.
The weight of other parts on the rotor is unbalanced. The solution is to check each part separately and adjust to balance.
Bearing clearance exceeding limit or damaged. The solution is to replace the bearings.
