During the growth of garlic, the nutrient requirements of nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium are more nitrogen and potassium, but less phosphorus. For every 1,000 kilograms of garlic tubers, about 4.8 kilograms of nitrogen, 1.4 kilograms of phosphorus, 4.4 kilograms of potassium, and 0.8 kilograms of sulfur are needed.
