News - What is the trend of industrial raw material prices in 2021?
What is the trend of industrial raw material prices in 2021?
Superimposed on the continuous rise of the Purchasing Managers Index (PMI) in November, it reflects that the current economic demand is still relatively strong. How long will the current rise in industrial products last, and how do you look at the changes in the prices of industrial products next year?
The logic of the price increase of industrial products in 2020 is the mismatch of global supply and demand under the impact of the epidemic. In 2021, after the epidemic is relatively well controlled, the relationship between supply and demand should not be as extreme as last year.
Judging from the practice of China’s producer price index (PPI), industrial product prices have a strong global resonance. China’s PPI is more consistent with the fluctuations of the import price index and the global energy and metal index, which requires a more global perspective.
There is a view that the recent increase in industrial product prices is related to the cold winter weather and increased heating demand. If you look at the same period in history, industrial products will indeed experience seasonal increases in December, but we can see from the month-on-month increase in the price of Nanhua’s industrial products that the month-on-month increase of 8.2% in December is far exceeding the historical average of 1.2%, showing an increase that exceeds seasonality.
We use the purchase price of the main raw materials in the PMI to make the difference with the ex-factory price and convert it into a year-on-year basis. As can be seen from the chart below, since May, the price increase of raw materials has continued to be higher than the ex-factory price.
