This is the policy (“privacy policy”) of MHALA regarding the privacy of information that we may collect through your use of our website. This privacy policy does not apply to information we may collect by any other method than through your use of the site.
For information about how MHALA treats any personal health information submitted by you in the course of using any of our services, please review the HIPAA Notice of Privacy Practice.
We collect personal information you choose to provide, which generally includes your name, email address, credit card information, postal address, billing address or information in comments that you provide. We also may maintain your responses to surveys and questionnaires that you may complete from time to time.
How We May Use Personal and Other Information
We also use information about your use of the site to improve the content of the site and to improve MHALA’s marketing and promotional efforts.
Any user or third party accessing the site or our services is responsible for its own use of the site and services. We are not responsible for any third party’s actions or its security controls with respect to information that third parties may collect or process via the site, services, or otherwise.
Please contact us if you have any questions or concerns about your personal information or require assistance in managing your choices.
Please be sure to include in any email your full name, email address, postal address, and any message. Please note that such requests may take up to thirty (30) days to become effective.
Additional Information If you have questions or concerns about our privacy policy or practices, please contact us at info@mhala.org.
