We have two needs lists on Amazon to facilitate your support of MHALA. One list supports our Antelope Valley programs while the other one supports our Long Beach programs.
To find out if your company has a matching gift policy, please enter your employer's name in the link below. If your company appears in the search results, follow the link or instructions provided.
You can help secure your legacy by making estate plan provisions to share a lasting, meaningful gift to individuals with mental health needs.
The most common planned gift is a bequest in your will or living trust. Others include annuities, charitable lead trusts, endowment funds, life insurance policies, retirement plan assets, real estate, and stocks and bonds.
Your financial advisor can help you decide which type of planned gift is best for you.
When you make a gift in memory of a loved one, you can provide an individual in your community with a life-changing opportunity to recover from their mental health challenges.
As you consider a gift of stock, let us know when and how we can expect to receive your donation. Standard stock transfer procedures do not often include information about the sender, so it can be hard to track who made the gift.
The gift will be valued at the average price in accordance with federal tax laws. Note that MHALA’s Tax ID number is 95-1881491.
Amazon will donate 0.5 percent of the price of eligible purchases each time you shop.
